 :nonclaims
 ["a capability with no declared effects is assumed to be a pure function of its arguments; that is a contract the catalog states and validates classification against, not something the kernel proves"
  "an operation result the journal's secret-stripping alters cannot be reconstructed, so such a session fails closed on resume rather than resuming with a different value; only data.json/read can produce such a result today"
  "a checkpoint still rewrites every form's source, so a very long session's journal remains quadratic in source bytes; receipts were kept out of the checkpoint for exactly this reason, but the existing growth was not addressed"
  "arguments outside the inert data domain are identified by type alone in the argument digest; such a call fails its operation's own validation and records the same failure either way"
  "one model, one endpoint, one live repetition; the live scenario is a demonstration that the path works end to end, not a measurement"
  "Linux x86_64 glibc only; no cross-platform or static-linking claim"
  "the image digest is an artifact identifier, not a reproducibility claim"
  "no JVM/native suite parity; the native evidence is the smoke, the authority corpus and the PTY gates"
